\f0\b\fs48 \cf2 \cb3 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Description\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs32 \cf2 \cb3 Implement batched real symmetric eigendecomposition.\cb1 \
\cb3 Input is 
\f2\fs28\fsmilli14400 \cb4 A
\f1\fs32 \cb3 , a 
\f2\fs28\fsmilli14400 \cb4 batch x n x n
\f1\fs32 \cb3  CUDA tensor in 
\f2\fs28\fsmilli14400 \cb4 torch.float32
\f1\fs32 \cb3 . Every input matrix is symmetric up to FP32 roundoff.\cb1 \
\cb3 Return 
\f2\fs28\fsmilli14400 \cb4 (Q, L)
\f1\fs32 \cb3  in the same eigenvector convention as 
\f2\fs28\fsmilli14400 \cb4 torch.linalg.eigh(A)
\f1\fs32 \cb3 : 
\f2\fs28\fsmilli14400 \cb4 Q
\f1\fs32 \cb3  is a 
\f2\fs28\fsmilli14400 \cb4 batch x n x n
\f1\fs32 \cb3  FP32 tensor whose columns are orthonormal eigenvectors, and 
\f2\fs28\fsmilli14400 \cb4 L
\f1\fs32 \cb3  is a 
\f2\fs28\fsmilli14400 \cb4 batch x n
\f1\fs32 \cb3  FP32 tensor of eigenvalues sorted in ascending order. The checker validates the invariant 
\f2\fs28\fsmilli14400 \cb4 A @ Q = Q @ diag(L)
\f1\fs32 \cb3 , reconstructs 
\f2\fs28\fsmilli14400 \cb4 A = Q @ diag(L) @ Q.T
\f1\fs32 \cb3 , and checks orthogonality of 
\f2\fs28\fsmilli14400 \cb4 Q
\f1\fs32 \cb3 .\cb1 \
\cb3 Eigenvectors are not unique. Individual signs may flip, and repeated or tightly clustered eigenvalues may rotate within their eigenspaces. Correctness is therefore based on matrix identities, not elementwise comparison against a reference eigensolver.\cb1 \
\cb3 This shape set mirrors the optimizer-statistics motivation in 
\f2\fs28\fsmilli14400 \cb4 qr_v2
\f1\fs32 \cb3 : square matrices produced from gradient views and second-moment style statistics. Batched 
\f2\fs28\fsmilli14400 \cb4 512 x 512
\f1\fs32 \cb3  is the central target, while 
\f2\fs28\fsmilli14400 \cb4 1024
\f1\fs32 \cb3 , 
\f2\fs28\fsmilli14400 \cb4 2048
\f1\fs32 \cb3 , and 
\f2\fs28\fsmilli14400 \cb4 4096
\f1\fs32 \cb3  cover larger square factors.\cb1 \
\cb3 Test and benchmark specs include a 
\f2\fs28\fsmilli14400 \cb4 cond
\f1\fs32 \cb3  field. In this task 
\f2\fs28\fsmilli14400 \cb4 cond
\f1\fs32 \cb3  is a deterministic dynamic-range knob, not an exact requested condition number. Some cases create spectra spanning 
\f2\fs28\fsmilli14400 \cb4 10^-cond
\f1\fs32 \cb3  to 
\f2\fs28\fsmilli14400 \cb4 1
\f1\fs32 \cb3 ; others apply row/column scaling or generate covariance-like positive semidefinite matrices. Stress cases include rank-deficient, near-rank-deficient, repeated-eigenvalue, clustered-eigenvalue, diagonal, banded, row-scaled, and mixed inputs. Correctness tests also include LAPACK DDRVST-inspired matrix types from 
\f2\fs28\fsmilli14400 \cb4 TESTING/EIG/ddrvst.f
\f1\fs32 \cb3 : zero, identity, diagonal spectra, dense planted-spectrum matrices, random symmetric matrices, and high- and low-magnitude banded variants.\cb1 \
\cb3 The 
\f2\fs28\fsmilli14400 \cb4 mixed
\f1\fs32 \cb3  case builds a heterogeneous batch: each matrix is independently assigned a conditioning profile at a random position in the batch. This mirrors real optimizer-statistics batches, where per-layer or per-block factors do not share one numerical structure. The benchmark set includes mixed batches and homogeneous ill-conditioned batches, so robustness is ranked, not only gated.\cb1 \
\cb3 Correctness is residual-gated against the original FP32 input. Low-bit FP16, FP8, or NVFP4 work is allowed as an internal implementation strategy: returned factors must still be FP32 and must represent a numerically meaningful eigendecomposition. Residuals are measured in FP64 to reduce checker noise, and the gates are intentionally dimension-scaled and invariant-based rather than elementwise reference comparisons. This leaves room for approximate low-bit solutions while still rejecting non-orthogonal factors, unsorted eigenvalues, and outputs that do not reconstruct the input. The hard gates are the eigen-equation residual 
\f2\fs28\fsmilli14400 \cb4 A @ Q - Q @ diag(L)
\f1\fs32 \cb3 , reconstruction residual 
\f2\fs28\fsmilli14400 \cb4 Q @ diag(L) @ Q.T - A
\f1\fs32 \cb3 , and orthogonality residual 
\f2\fs28\fsmilli14400 \cb4 Q.T @ Q - I
\f1\fs32 \cb3 , each applied relative to the corresponding matrix L1 norm.\cb1 \
\cb3 Among passing submissions, ranking is by runtime using the geometric mean of benchmark cases.\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

